// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Stabilizer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3742359945" "Dimensional stabilizer"
// DetailString :
"P310836346" "This thin, silver wand looks a lot more like a TV antenna than a highly sophisticated technical device. With any luck, it'll allow you to close the dimensional ruptures linking your world to others."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Stabilizer2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1998666384" "Dimensional Band-Aids"
// DetailString :
"P1223349564" "These thin metal disks must be placed at the location of the dimensional ruptures. Though they won't close the rupture entirely, they'll keep it too small for matter to travel between dimensions. Portal Corporation scientists hope that keeping these ruptures partially open will prevent new ruptures from cropping up on other dimensions."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P214314430" "{HeroName}, I've been asked to bring you into the loop on one of the big security issues around here. Can't say I'm happy about it, but maybe you'll make me eat those words. I just hope all the good things I've heard about you are true. <br><br>It seems these scientists bit off a little more than they can chew when they designed these portals. They've been doing their best to keep things under control, but every once in a while, a dimensional rupture crops up. A little schism in the dimensional fabric. If we can't stay on top of them, these ruptures could put our entire world at risk. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Someone's got to close those ruptures, and you're the hero for the job.</A><br><br>I have to warn you, things could get tricky. We may find ourselves dealing with limited time here."
// AcceptString :
"P165239140" "Close the dimensional ruptures"
// SendOffString :
"P1689637613" "We've located a number of ruptures linking our world to that of the Banished Pantheon. You'll have to go there to seal them up."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound1_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P920164289" "Every one of those dimensional ruptures has to be closed!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3530989997" "Tales of the Banished Pantheon's world have become popular horror stories around Portal Corporation."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Ruptures 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P3794478536" "Dimensional rupture"
// Description :
"P3931324677" "ruptures to close"
// SingularDescription :
"P1158884718" "Close the last rupture!"
// InteractBeginString :
"P1928151685" "You begin to close the rupture."
// InteractInterruptedString :
"P2557807414" "You have been interrupted!"
// InteractCompleteString :
"P1243594045" "You have closed the rupture."
// InteractActionString :
"P19986288" "Closing..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2292430725" "You have closed all the dimensional ruptures."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound1_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3788043235" "Return to contact"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1727263063" "I need your report in person, soldier."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P330008341" "Nicely done, {HeroName}, but your job isn't over yet. I just spoke to one of the techies, and it looks like some new ruptures have cropped up on another world. Trouble is, this is one of the restricted dimensions: Omega Omicron 26-20, the Council Empire."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound1_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P697941137" "If those dimensional ruptures stay open, we may have a Council invasion on our hands!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P255277008" "The Council of this world has worked hard to secure their dominion over the former United States. They're just now beginning to clean up the detritus of war."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Ruptures2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound1_Part4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1160840399" "Report to me in person at once."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P459593867" "This isn't looking good, {HeroName}. It seems that every time you close one of these ruptures, another one opens. The scientists think that some sort of permanent damage may have happened to the dimensional fabric. It's going to require some study, but for now they've come up with a quick and dirty fix: these new gadgets. Their official name is 'spatial stabilimeters,' but I heard some of the techies calling them 'dimensional Band-Aids.' That name works for me. <br><br>If you can't get these Band-Aids in place quickly, though, we may have even more problems. The techs tell me the ruptures could become permanent."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound1_Part5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1522179960" "I need those ruptures dealt with, on the double!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P905499747" "The clear night sky provides a hauntingly beautiful backdrop to these desolate ruins."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Ruptures3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P3104962594" "ruptures to patch"
// SingularDescription :
"P763962970" "Patch the last rupture!"
// InteractBeginString :
"P2309026104" "You begin to patch the rupture."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P2598438997" "You have patched the rupture."
// InteractActionString :
"P1135525675" "Patching..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3409628169" "You have patched all the dimensional ruptures."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1257070273" "Some of the ruptures have become permanent."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2166355866" "Here's a dimensional stabilizer. The crew here at Portal Corporation cooked it up just a few days ago. Let's hope it's as good as they say it is."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P963336352" "Got to say, I'm impressed. You handled everything those dimensions could throw at you. But from what the techies tell me, this case is far from over. You may have managed to patch up the ruptures, but there's an underlying problem that still needs fixing. When Portal Corporation has a permanent fix ready, I'll know who to call on for help."
// RandomFameString :
"P1567982399" "I hear Unai Kemen really trusts {HeroName}. That's quite a testimonial!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2518246" "The technicians tell me some of those portals may have become permanent. That's a bad thing. We'll do what we can to repair the damage, but I may need more help from you in the future."
// RandomFameString :
"P1830726344" "I hear {HeroName}'s had a bit of bad luck out in the multi-verse."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Kit 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2207636026" "Medical kit"
// DetailString :
"P2780393188" "This medical kit contains several dozen syringes with extra sharp needles, meant for piercing the Hydra Men's tough hide and extracting their blood. Each syringe is designed to deliver a dose of antibiotics upon insertion, to prevent any accidental harm to the Hydra Men."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DNA 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P884797359" "DNA samples"
// DetailString :
"P1117044955" "Your medical kit now contains samples of DNA from a large selection of Hydra Men. You only wish you could have taken them peacefully."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1044467430" "I've got a situation I'd like you to handle, {HeroName}. The Rikti have unleashed a biological weapon on a large section of Founders' Falls. Lots of people are sick, and the doctors aren't getting anywhere. They only thing they've determined for sure is that the disease is linked to Hydra Man DNA. Dr. Steven Sheridan needs a wide sample of the DNA in order to begin figuring out a cure. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>I need you to get to the Hydra dimension and get some samples of their DNA.</A> It may be our only chance of saving the Rikti's victims."
// AcceptString :
"P3162460182" "Get some samples of Hydra Man DNA"
// SendOffString :
"P59668120" "It's been determined that the Hydra Men are the innocent victims of the Rikti's machinations. Do what you have to do to get those samples, but take care to cause no permanent harm."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound2_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1838947028" "Take samples from all Hydra Men"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2799374559" "This is a life or death situation, {HeroName}. I need that DNA, and I need it now!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3245340291" "You can't help but feel sorry for the Hydra Men, the peaceful victims of the Rikti war effort. If you can get the DNA peacefully, you'll jump at the chance. If you can't, you'll use utmost caution."
// Script Variable PATROLLER1_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P856364347" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3856321543" "You got enough samples of Hydra Man DNA."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound2_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P212396353" "Take samples to Dr. Sheridan"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1086742040" "Dr. Sheridan can start working on a cure as soon as you get him those samples."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P650065917" "Good job, {HeroName}. These samples you took from the Hydra Men should help us not only construct a cure for the Rikti's new plague, but a vaccine as well. It's too bad you had to take them from the Hydra Men by force. If only I could devise some way of communicating with those creatures! Perhaps then they could find some consolation in the fact that they're helping to foil a plot cooked up by their Rikti kidnappers!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4220782937" "Here's a medical kit. You should be able to collect enough samples with this."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3929129808" "Dr. Sheridan has already had great progress with his cure for the Rikti plague. I must say, you performed admirably in a tough situation. Quick, efficient, and with no permanent damage to any Hydra Men. I'm glad to have worked with you on this."
// RandomFameString :
"P1547256107" "{HeroName} helped stop a Rikti plague!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Inscription 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3559772569" "Nemesis' epitaph"
// DetailString :
"P2962527861" "The epitaph on the obelisk read: <br><br>'I no longer have any hope of saving myself from this despicable disease. One thought alone consoles me: my creations will not allow a single thing to survive me. They will rule this world forever, alone, in the name of Nemesis.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P4040610978" "{HeroName}, I've got a job for you to do. Portal Corporation just located a new dimension. We're calling it Tau Delta 8-7 for right now, but the first person to explore it gets to choose the unofficial name. If you're up for it, that could be you. What do you say? <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Want to explore a brand new dimension?</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P3733188384" "Explore the new dimension"
// SendOffString :
"P2083389344" "When I say brand new, of course, I merely mean newly discovered. This world has had millennia to develop and grow on its own. It's possible you'll find just about anything there, so be on your guard."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound3_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2879585319" "Investigate the new dimension"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4099639457" "I want to know all about that new dimension!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3053379487" "You hear a strangely unemotional voice say, 'I need to see those TPS reports.'"
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2726548472" "Who made the coffee this morning?"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2896325815" "Did someone park in my employee of the month spot?"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P559276206" "Nemesis security breached! Repel all invaders with maximum force!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3264133048" "I need to see those TPS reports."
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P979819998" "Did anyone see the game last night?"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3512413878" "We will defend Nemesis forever!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2564058557" "Nemesis can never be defeated!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3545081826" "Nemesis is forever!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3956336154" "Worn Warhulk"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2069623099" "Nemesis is our master. We must defend his domain!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P685970202" "You will never stop Nemesis!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Obelisk 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P857191801" "Coffin"
// Description :
"P480797583" "Seek clues"
// InteractBeginString :
"P1968078055" "You begin to read the epitaph."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P4265284745" "You have read the epitaph."
// InteractActionString :
"P752952337" "Reading..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2654594785" "This coffin contains the unburied body of Nemesis."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P376058582" "You learned the secrets of this strange new dimension."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound3_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4040847099" "I need to know everything you've learned about that new dimension. You had better report in person for debriefing."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3180562069" "There was nothing left on that world but old Nemesis automatons? What happened to all the people? I think we have to assume that the Nemesis of Tau Delta 8-7 did something terrible to his world. {HeroName}, I think you should go back. It could be that there are still people there in hiding, but they can't come out for fear of the automatons. If we allow Nemesis' leftover robots to run rampant across that planet, it'll be a dead world forever. <br><br>There have to be some sort of refueling machines in the area; even Nemesis' steam-powered creations can't run forever without some system for refilling their resevoirs. I need you to find those machines and eliminate them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound3_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3782576761" "Disable refueling machines"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P921287489" "I want you to disassemble every machine in that area."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P879228068" "The lively chirps of the Nemesis automatons grate against your ears."
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1757941104" "Nemesis is king!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1845560031" "You cannot hope to battle the army of Nemesis!"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P820365916" "Repel the invaders! Nemesis security must be ensured!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1528069394" "Nemesis is all!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Generators 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P3550872253" "Refueling machine"
// Description :
"P1091067233" "machines to disable"
// SingularDescription :
"P1656225752" "Disable the last machine!"
// InteractBeginString :
"P2652292300" "You begin to disable the machine."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P4199121765" "You have disabled the machine."
// InteractActionString :
"P852563986" "Disabling..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2746309638" "You destroyed the refueling machine."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3351786754" "Good work, {HeroName}. I'll keep sending heroes to dimension Tau Delta 8-7, until we get the entire planet cleared of automatons. If there's one thing I've learned in this job, it's this: even if it's on another world, you never, ever leave a doomsday device in working order."
// RandomFameString :
"P1280612320" "I hear {HeroName} went to a world where nothing was left! Nothing but Nemesis robots, that is."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Mission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Blockers 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P894716963" "Psychic blocker"
// DetailString :
"P2257091341" "It would be hard for you to say whether this small metal disk operates by magic, science, or a mixture of the two. When placed on a large Clockwork robot, it should produce a signal that keeps the Clockwork King's energies confined to his own wasted dimension."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P914798374" "People around here are getting pretty antsy about dimension Epsilon Tau 27-2. That's the dimension ruled over by the ultra-powerful Clockwork King. With all the dimensional ruptures that have been happening lately, there's a concern that Epsilon Tau's King may start extending his psychic tendrils into our own dimension. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>I need you to go to his dimension and set up a psychic blocker.</A> That should keep him in check."
// AcceptString :
"P336161940" "Set up the psychic blocker"
// SendOffString :
"P3963884998" "I'm sure you remember all the trouble this dimension's Clockwork King caused. We can't have another, more powerful King on our hands!"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P110207890" "Find biggest Clockwork"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4083579430" "I need that psychic blocker placed, {HeroName}. We have to prevent a psychic incursion into this dimension."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1043439269" "You have a sense of unease as you step onto the ruined landscape of Clockwork Earth."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2840667635" "Babbage"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Babbage 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P3694013659" "Place blocker on Babbage"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2980253524" "This psychic blocker is powered by psychic energy. I want you to find the biggest, baddest Clockwork you can and put the blocker on him. That way we can be certain it'll stay active for a good long while."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3964880355" "You placed all the psychic blockers."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3589104272" "You faced the Babbage of Clockwork Earth? And you lived to tell about it? {HeroName}, I'm impressed. With that psychic blocker in place on Clockwork Earth, we shouldn't have to fear any psychic meddling from that world's Clockwork King. It's clear that all the things I've heard about you were right. You know how to get the job done."
// RandomFameString :
"P3401957606" "I hear {HeroName} went back to Clockwork Earth!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Mission5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2941565144" "We've got a tense situation here, {HeroName}. One of Portal Corporation's own scientists has been kidnapped by the Council. Not the Council of this world; the Council of dimension Omega Omicron 26-20: the Council Empire! Dr. Sam Naples is not only too nice a guy to leave at the Council's mercy, he's also the biggest brain we've got around here. He knows more about the dimensional ruptures than anybody. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>You've got to rescue Dr. Naples from the Council Empire.</A> There's a lot riding on this one."
// AcceptString :
"P1331692011" "Rescue Dr. Naples from the Council Empire"
// SendOffString :
"P2438765254" "I don't know whether the Coucnil is looking for info on these dimensional ruptures, but I'd say it's a good bet."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2398369625" "Find Dr. Sam Naples"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2186731752" "Dr. Naples' fate is in your hands. And possibly that of the multiverse!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2074222366" "The Council Empire is one of the restricted dimensions for good reason. The fiends who dominate this world would love to get their hands on your own dimension."
// Script Variable PATROLLER1_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P4040920331" "Naples has a lot of useful information."
// Script Variable PATROLLER2_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P4171483521" "Indeed."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P771238011" "Dr. Sam Naples"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1600184393" "My brethren, Portal Corporation's secrets will soon be yours."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1439612965" "You think you can take on a whole world of my brothers? Hah! Be my guest!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Naples 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3723908958" "You defeated Dr. Naples."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3908604349" "Well, I did some checking, and it looks like Dr. Naples' real name is Julius Pazzi. He was a scientist all right, but he was never interested in exploration of new dimensions. He was interested in getting his hands on as much Portal Corporation data as the Council could use. We'll have to keep our eye on the Council Empire from now on, {HeroName}. There's no telling how much information Naples managed to pass on before you apprehended him."
// RandomFameString :
"P3822328923" "I hear {HeroName} unmasked a Council spy!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_Portal_Compound6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CarnieStory 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P314271267" "Mistress Kay's story"
// DetailString :
"P1101746048" "When you rescued Mistress Kay from the Praetorians, she told you: <br><br>'The villain Neuron has already begun his plan to flood Paragon City with dimensional ruptures. He has set up his equipment on a remote dimension; without the proper coordinates, you could never find it in time. Go swiftly, and take care of yourself. You are your world's best hope of survival."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2484932744" "We just got a call for help from the strangest of sources: the Carnival of Shadows! Well, actually, the Carnival of Light. It seems that on Praetorian Earth, Vanessa DeVore is actually one of the good guys. She's claiming that Neuron, one of the Praetorian supervillains, has hatched a plan to open up dimensional ruptures all over Paragon City. If he manages to do it, it'll be a madhouse: strange creatures and crazed villains wandering around every city block. Vanessa's willing to help us, but we have to help her first. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>You have to save some of her carnies from the Praetorians.</A> It's the only way to get the information we need."
// AcceptString :
"P2750927216" "Save the carnies from the Praetorians"
// SendOffString :
"P1284078805" "It feels weird to trust Vanessa DeVore about anything, but all signs indicate that she's shooting straight."

